From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:39:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: server item configs set stockmarket instead of tradeable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Two things kept `ItemServerType.tradeable` at its default `true` for items that `items.toml`
marks `tradeable = false` (coal bag, looting bag, quest items, ...).

1. `ItemServerCodec.createData` copies an item's server config entry over the cache data, but it assigns the
   entry's `tradeable` to `stockmarket`:

       stockmarket = customData.tradeable

   So `tradeable` was never set, and every item with a config entry but no `tradeable` line was put on the Grand
   Exchange (`stockmarket = true`), whatever the cache says (coins, for example).

2. Fixing the codec alone changes nothing in an existing cache. `PackServerConfig` repacks a type only when its
   fingerprint changes (its toml files' contents, the base archive's CRC). A codec change is not part of it, so
   `buildCache` keeps the item archive packed by the old codec. Touching `items.toml` does not help either: the
   fingerprint hashes file contents, not timestamps.

Change. `tradeable = customData.tradeable`; `stockmarket` keeps the cache's value. Each server config pack type
gets a `codecVersion` (default 1) that goes into its incremental fingerprint. Items are at 2, so existing caches
repack the item archive once. Bump it whenever a codec packs the same inputs differently.

Tests. New `ItemServerCodecTest` (`:or-cache:test`): a config entry with `tradeable = false` makes the item
untradeable; an entry without it keeps a non-GE item off the GE and a GE item on it. The first two fail before
the codec change. For the fingerprint, checked on an existing cache: before, after the codec change and a
`buildCache`, the packed SERVER cache still read coal bag `tradeable=true` and coins `stockmarket=true`. After
the `codecVersion` change, one `buildCache` repacked the item archive and the cache reads coal bag and looting bag
`tradeable=false`, coins `stockmarket=false` and lobster `stockmarket=true`. A looting bag test that stores a coal
bag fails on the old cache and passes on the new one. The TOML decode itself was fine: decoding the real
`items.toml` gives `tradeable=false` for these entries, `inherit` included.

Caveats. Behaviour changes for every item with a config entry. Items the cache does not list on the Grand
Exchange stop counting as `stockmarket`. Items marked `tradeable = false` become untradeable for the code that
checks it (death drops, the guide-price interface through `ocTradable`, shops that check
`tradeable || stockmarket`). That is the intended data, but anything that relied on the old values is worth a
look. The first `buildCache` after this repacks every server config type once, because the new fingerprint key
changes all their fingerprints.

